    {
      "id": "p0078-b004",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Even though Toby’s reference to Mt. Itoi would be lost on Japanese players, the reference to Toby’s name could still be conveyed in translation. To make the reference work, the translator took the name トビイ (to bi i, “Toby”), reversed the characters, and called the mountain “Mt. Ibito”.",
        "raw": "Even though Toby's reference to Mt. Itoi would be lost on Japanese players, the\nreference to Toby's name could still be conveyed in translation. To make the\nreference work, the translator took the name I-1::''1 (to bi i, \"Toby\"), reversed\nthe characters, and called the mountain \"Mt. Ibito\".",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en",
          "ja"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29851278,
          0.7505,
          0.90352387,
          0.8169
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.29050692,
          0.74978571,
          0.90555581,
          0.81797143
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          44,
          45,
          46,
          47
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "日本玩家虽然看不出对 Mt. Itoi 的致敬，但对 Toby 名字的指涉仍能译出来。译者采用トビイ（to bi i，即 Toby 的日文写法），将字符倒过来，把山命名为“Mt. Ibito”。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 58,
            "italic": true,
            "lang": "en"
          }
        ]
      },
      "annotations": [],
      "layout": {
